 ## Overview
-Polynomial Basis Vector Generation constructs the explicit monomial basis vector for a given spatial point and polynomial degree [S1, unofficial]. It serves as the foundational step for the Basis Transform for Trivariate Polynomials, enabling the conversion of B-spline coefficients into a form suitable for efficient root finding and volume compositing [S1, unofficial]. Unlike methods that store full polynomial descriptions, this method generates the basis vector on-the-fly or caches it, avoiding the memory overhead of storing every single polynomial's coefficients explicitly [S1, unofficial]. It is distinct from the Basis Matrix Generation variant, which aggregates these vectors into a matrix structure for batch processing [S1, unofficial].
